WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.229 --> 00:00:05.230
Hello, my name is Edward Bennet and I'm an instructor here at Epic Games.

2
00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:10.230
Welcome to Introduction to Blueprints for Unreal Engine 5.3.

3
00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:16.230
This course is a great starting-off point if you haven't done much programming before

4
00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:19.230
and you are not used to using the engine.

5
00:00:19.230 --> 00:00:23.230
At the end of this, we hope to give you all of the foundations that will allow you to

6
00:00:23.230 --> 00:00:28.230
go on and become a more advanced programmer within the Blueprint system.

7
00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:35.229
Our goals from this is to familiarize you with all of the terminology and programming

8
00:00:35.229 --> 00:00:39.229
concepts that you're going to need to get started.

9
00:00:39.229 --> 00:00:44.229
We're not going to go too deep, we're going to give you enough to be moving on with.

10
00:00:44.229 --> 00:00:50.229
And then we want you to have a good understanding of how Blueprints fit into Unreal Engine,

11
00:00:50.229 --> 00:00:54.229
where they can be found and how they can be used.

12
00:00:54.229 --> 00:00:56.229
Lastly, we'll do an exercise.

13
00:00:56.229 --> 00:01:01.229
And if you follow along with this exercise, you should get a good foundation on how to

14
00:01:01.229 --> 00:01:05.230
create and write your own scripts within the engine.

15
00:01:05.230 --> 00:01:10.230
Then you'll understand all of the different buttons and all of the different sections of the interface.

16
00:01:10.230 --> 00:01:15.230
This should act as a good foundation to future learning.
